   165	| hard | four further seeds | Gemini 3.8 Flash | API errors; unscored |
   166	
   167	| G9 arm | solved / attempts | conclusion |
   168	|---|---:|---|
   169	| bare | 0/1 scored | first hard answer failed; remaining calls blocked by quota |
   170	| structural hint | 0/0 scored | all retries errored; diagnostic unavailable |
   171	| placebo | 0/0 scored | all retries errored; diagnostic unavailable |
   172	
   173	Consequently hinted-minus-placebo is recorded as `null`, not as a fabricated
   174	zero.  These arms are diagnostic under the current contract; G9's actual gate
   175	is the size/effort cap, which passes.  A funded OpenRouter key is still required
   176	to complete STEP 4 and the three diagnostics, then update `G9_RESULTS` and
   177	regenerate `selftest_report.json`.
   178	
   179	## Use
   180	
   181	```python
   182	from gen_2003_00668 import DIFFICULTY, make_instance, render, verify
   183	
   184	inst = make_instance(seed=7, **DIFFICULTY["hard"])
   185	print(render(inst))
   186	ok, reason = verify(inst, inst["answer"])
   187	assert (ok, reason) == (True, "ok")
   188	```
   189	
   190	From the repository root, after completing the interrupted oracle runs:
   191	
   192	```bash
   193	bash scripts/emit.sh 2003.00668 20 hard
   194	```
   195	
   196	## Caveats
   197	
   198	The family is easy with exact linear-algebra software, by design and as Track B
   199	declares.  The 0/200,000 guess result samples uniformly from the explicitly
   200	required full-support normalized vectors; it is not a claim about arbitrary
   201	model priors or about average-case coding-theory hardness.  The adversary panel
   202	tests a multiplier outlier, first-moment greedy repair, constant, alternating,
   203	and linear progression ansatzes, and 256 random restarts, but not every possible
   204	symbolic interpolation heuristic.  In particular, a solver that recognizes
   205	the barycentric/binomial identity has found the intended route.
   206	
   207	`canonical_key` exactly handles input-row permutations and nonzero row scalings,
   208	physical-qudit and canonical-hyperbolic-pair permutations, affine changes of the
   209	evaluation variable, equivalent rescalings of transvection vectors, and their composition.
   210	Full equivalence of linear codes under arbitrary row operations and monomial
   211	symplectic maps is not canonicalized; computing that equivalence is outside the
   212	cheap duplicate check, so the key uses the strongest exact normal form for the
   213	generator's own relabellings.  Finally, no shipping claim should be trusted
   214	until the currently blocked bare run has a `hardened` verdict.  The hinted and
   215	placebo arms are informative diagnostics rather than gates, but they also remain
   216	unmeasured because of the same quota exhaustion.

