Implemented a native Track B symplectic-radical problem family based on Section II of the [paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2003.00668).

Deliverables:

- [gen_2003_00668.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.00668/gen_2003_00668.py:1)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.00668/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.00668/README.md:1)
- [bare oracle transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.00668/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.00668/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2003.00668/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local verification passes all nine gates:

- 0/200,000 random-candidate hits in a 343-bit answer space.
- Six attacks failed across 8/8 seeds each.
- Reference Gaussian algorithm solved 8/8, requiring 12,150,796 counted operations.
- Answer: 59 atoms, 226 characters, 119 conservative tokens.
- Compact route: 291 exact operations.
- Independent Gram-rank/kernel checks passed on 12 additional instances.

The result is not yet shippable because OpenRouter exhausted its total quota during STEP 4. Easy was solved 3/3, medium 2/3, and the first hard attempt failed verification; subsequent hard, hinted, and placebo calls were unscored HTTP 403 errors. The transcripts and README record this without claiming a hardened verdict. Completing the task requires replenishing the OpenRouter quota and rerunning the three harness arms.
